    "evidence_text": "Miss Albany Diner\n\nNew Bay Diner Restaurant\n\nThe New Bay Diner Restaurant is a historic diner at 950 Bay Street in Springfield, Massachusetts.\n\nWilliam Wallace Atterbury\n\n He was also known as \"The Railroad General\".\n\nCorner Lunch\n\nThe Corner Lunch Diner is a historic diner at 133 Lamartine Street in Worcester, Massachusetts.\n\n It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2000.\n\nRosie's Diner\n\nRosie's Diner is located in Cedar Springs, Michigan.\n\n A third diner was later moved to the site from Fulton, New York.\n\n A series of replicas were built as part of a chain of restaurants in the Denver area.\n\nSam's Diner\n\nMunson Diner\n\nMunson Diner is a historic diner located at Liberty in Sullivan County, New York.\n\n It has a riveted steel frame and exterior of stainless steel and porcelain enamel.\n\nIronweed (film)\n\nTricentennial Park (Albany, New York)\n\nLark Street\n\nLark Street is a historic street in Albany, New York, USA.\n\n Lark Street and Jay Street was used as a location during the filming of \"Ironweed\".",
